se,"module_direction":"lower in AD","module_padj":0.446504,"module_significant":false},{"cell_type":"OPC","gene_id":"ENSG00000139644","module":"royalblue","kme":0.332325,"hub":true,"module_direction":"higher in AD","module_padj":0.683527,"module_significant":false},{"cell_type":"Oli","gene_id":"ENSG00000139644","module":"turquoise","kme":0.220436,"hub":false,"module_direction":"higher in AD","module_padj":0.415372,"module_significant":false}],"degas_bulk_de":false,"drug_target":false}},"description":[{"gene_id":"ENSG00000139644","entrez_id":["7009"],"uniprot":["P55061"],"ncbi_summary":"Enables endoribonuclease inhibitor activity and ubiquitin protein ligase binding activity. Involved in several processes, including negative regulation of RNA metabolic process; negative regulation of intrinsic apoptotic signaling pathway; and response to L-glutamate. Acts upstream of or within negative regulation of calcium ion transport into cytosol. Located in endoplasmic reticulum membrane and mitochondrial membrane. Biomarker of cervical squamous cell carcinoma and prostate carcinoma. [provided by Alliance of Genome Resources, Apr 2022]","ncbi_source":"NCBI Gene summary (RefSeq), via MyGene.info","uniprot_function":[{"accession":"P55061","text":"Endoplasmic reticulum (ER)-resident protein that confers cellular protection as an anti-apoptotic protein by limiting multiple stress-inducing pathways surrounding the endoplasmic reticulum and mitochondria (PubMed:21075086, PubMed:21068390). Inhibits the activities of the key sensor for the endoplasmic reticulum unfolded protein response IRE1alpha/ERN1 both directly and by blocking BAX/BAK binding (PubMed:19328063). Modulates ER calcium homeostasis by acting as a calcium-leak channel (PubMed:22128171). Negatively regulates autophagy and autophagosome formation, especially during periods of nutrient deprivation, and reduces cell survival during starvation (By similarity)."}],"uniprot_source":"UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot Function, release 2026_03","retrieved":"2026-10-21"}],"structures":[],"alphafold_accessions":[]}